{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-job-17-1","title":"Job 17:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Job appeals from men to God. 6 The unmerciful dealing of men with the afflicted may astonish, but not discourage the righteous. 11 His hope is not in life, but in death.</p>\n<p>breath is corrupt. or, spirit is spent. 19:17 my days. 6:11; 42:16; Isa 57:16 the graves. 13,14; Ps 88:3-5; Isa 38:10-14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-17-2","title":"Job 17:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>mockers. 12:4; 13:9; 16:20; 21:3; Ps 35:14-16; Mt 27:39-44 continue. Heb. lodge. Ps 25:13; 91:1; *marg: provocation. 1Sa 1:6,7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-17-3","title":"Job 17:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>put me. 9:33; Ge 43:9; 44:32; Pr 11:15; 20:16; Heb 7:22 strike. Pr 6:11; 11:15; *marg: Pr 17:18; 22:26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-17-4","title":"Job 17:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>2Sa 15:31; 17:14; 2Ch 25:16; Isa 19:14; Mt 11:25; 13:11; Ro 11:8 1Co 1:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-17-5","title":"Job 17:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>He that. 32:21,22; Ps 12:2,3; Pr 20:19; 29:5; 1Th 2:5 the eyes. Ex 20:5; De 28:65; 1Ki 11:12; La 4:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-17-6","title":"Job 17:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>a by-word. 30:9; 1Ki 9:7; Ps 44:14 aforetime. or, before them. as a tabret. Ge 31:27; Isa 5:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-17-7","title":"Job 17:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Mine eye. 16:16; Ps 6:7; 31:9,10; La 5:17 members. or, thoughts. 11 shadow. Ps 109:23; Ec 6:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-17-8","title":"Job 17:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>astonied. Ps 73:12-15; Ec 5:8; Hab 1:13; Ro 11:33 stir up. 34:30; Ac 13:46</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-17-9","title":"Job 17:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>hold on. Ps 84:7,11; Pr 4:18; 14:16; Isa 35:8-10; 1Pe 1:5; 1Jo 2:19 clean. Ge 20:5; Ps 24:4; 26:6; 73:13; Isa 1:15,16; Mr 7:2 be stronger and stronger. Heb. add strength. Isa 40:29-31; 2Co 12:9,10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-17-10","title":"Job 17:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>do ye return. 6:29; Mal 3:18 for I. 4; 15:9; 32:9; 42:7; 1Co 1:20; 6:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-17-11","title":"Job 17:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>My days. 7:6; 9:25,26; Isa 38:10 purposes. Pr 16:9; 19:21; Ec 9:10; Isa 8:10; La 3:37; Ro 1:13; 2Co 1:15-17 Jas 4:13-15 thoughts. Heb. possessions.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-17-12","title":"Job 17:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>change. 7:3,4,13,14; 24:14-16; De 28:67 short. Heb. near.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-17-13","title":"Job 17:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>If I wait. 14:14; Ps 27:14; La 3:25,26 the grave. 1; 10:21,22; 30:23 I have made. Ps 139:8; Isa 57:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-17-14","title":"Job 17:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>said. Heb. cried, or, called. corruption. 21:32,33; Ps 16:10; 49:9; Ac 2:27-31; 13:34-37; 1Co 15:42,53,54 to the worm. 19:26; 24:20; Isa 14:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-17-15","title":"Job 17:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>my hope. 4:6; 6:11; 13:15; 19:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-17-16","title":"Job 17:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>the bars of the pit. 18:13,14; 33:18-28; Ps 88:4-8; 143:7; Isa 38:17,18; Jon 2:6 rest. 3:17-19; Eze 37:11; 2Co 1:9</p>"}]}